WEBVTT

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.830
Maria Watches Over Us

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:16.140
Spreading a blank map wide open
Shiroi chizu ookiku hiroge

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:23.120
Let's go hide the treasure box
Takara-bako kakushi ni ikou

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:31.190
No need for coats or even hats
Kooto nante iranai boushi mo ne

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:38.830
Armed with just mechanical pencil lead
Shaapen no shin dake haite

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.240
Round and round and round,
Kururu kururu ku

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.140
Running through
kakenukeru

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.110
Round and round and round,
Kururu kururu ku

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:54.070
Our footprints mark the X
ashiato wa batsu-jirushi da yo

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:01.090
Passing through the walls of the school
Kousha no kabe tsuki-nuke

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:09.330
We can go anywhere, there will be a path there
Dokonimo ikeru soko ni michi ga aru

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:16.530
The pleats of our skirts won't be disturbed
Sukaato no hida midare-nai

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:23.870
If it's a secret journey
Himitsu no tabi nara

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:39.820
A quarter till...

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:42.120
I might be a bit early.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.560
Morning, Yumi.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.070
G-Good morning, Onee-sama.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.270
Uh, but...

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.440
I was so excited, I woke up early.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:59.210
And I was in such an eager rush,
I ended up arriving early.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.840
You... were excited?

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:06.580
You know how they often say you
wake up before the alarm on golf day?

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.150
Maybe it was like that.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:15.130
Members of my household told me
to have the car drive us.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.190
I had such a hard time turning them down.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.700
The car...

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.570
They just don't understand.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.910
Swaying together with you on packed trains...

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.580
...and getting lost at the transfer
stations are what makes it fun.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.940
You think... that's fun?

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.350
It will be fun.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.340
With the two of us together, I am sure of it.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.410
Onee-sama...

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.990
How crowded the trains are
will be out of our hands,

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:45.730
but we can still be smart about
choosing which car to get on.

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.520
And I will be certain...

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:52.990
...not to get us lost!

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:58.040
The Red Rose's Sigh

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:00.610
Women Only

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:01.910
Women Only
"Atama-tori."

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:02.640
Women Only
"A," right? Then " aria."

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.170
"A," right? Then " aria."

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.020
"A"..." A"..." Furiijia (freesia)."

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.750
"Fuufu (married couple)."

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:07.980
Why are my dear sister and
I on a train on a weekday?
"Fuufu (married couple)."

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:08.220
Why are my dear sister and
I on a train on a weekday?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.020
Why are my dear sister and
I on a train on a weekday?
"Fu"...

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.020
Why are my dear sister and
I on a train on a weekday?

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.350
Why are my dear sister and
I on a train on a weekday?
"Fu"..." Fu"...

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.020
It all began with a certain
comment from my dear sister.
"Fu"..." Fu"...

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.320
It all began with a certain
comment from my dear sister.
"Sukaafu (scarf)"!

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:14.810
It all began with a certain
comment from my dear sister.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.450
Final exams are depressing.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.030
Yoshino, you have a tendency
to want to skip subjects...

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.760
...the worse you are at them.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.470
I plan something to do after the exams are over.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.870
It strangely motivates me.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.510
You're going on a little excursion
to see Buddhist statues, right?

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.080
Yes.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.810
That's it! I just have to come up with a reward!

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.890
I want to go on a trip somewhere
during exam break!

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.510
Oh, hey, what about you, Yumi-san?

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.190
Where do you want to go?

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:48.850
What?

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.520
Let's all just go somewhere!

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:55.030
Then, shall we go to the
amusement park during exam break?

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:57.590
Huh?

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.390
What did you just say?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.410
"Shall we go to the amusement park?"
That is what I said.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.270
Um...

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:09.380
"Let us go to the amusement
park after final exams are over."

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:10.640
Is that what you meant?

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.580
That is what I have been saying from the start.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.870
However, I am not riding any roller coasters.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.590
I'm so happy! I'm so happy!
I don't know what to do!

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:26.490
Um, how do everyone else's schedules look?

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.800
Does anyone not like amusement parks?

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:29.820
Yumi.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.700
Pardon me.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:34.500
I do not know what you are
pardoning yourself for,

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.900
but we are going to the
amusement park just the two of us.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:37.840
What?

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.500
Obviously.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.500
W-What? Then, might that mean?

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.110
Might that mean what?

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.340
Uh, well...

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.080
There was no "might" about it. It was a date!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.750
I got teased a lot by
Yoshino-san after that, though.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:54.780
Yumi.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.950
Oh, yes?

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.490
The word is "suraisu (slice)."

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:00.660
Oh, let me think...

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:01.660
"Rirakkusu (relax)."

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.700
"Rinri (ethics)."

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.630
"Ri"...

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.070
Wait, um, Onee-sama,

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.100
is it just me...

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.900
...or have you been choosing words
that start and end in the same letter?

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.170
Oh, did you notice?

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:15.840
So you were making me do all the thinking.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.400
But it did serve to exercise your brain, didn't it?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:32.550
What?

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:35.850
Why?
Why?

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.530
Kashiwagi-san...

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.140
And Yuki?

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.230
Hey there.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.870
What are you doing here?!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.710
I'd like to know that, too.

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:50.840
That's not an answer!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:53.880
Suguru-san, what is the meaning of this?

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:58.850
I believe I respectfully
declined your escort yesterday.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.290
Of course, I heard you.

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.390
Then what are you doing here?

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:03.980
Something wrong with me being here?

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:08.460
You're not going to say we can't go
into this amusement park, are you?

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.620
All right.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:16.960
So, you came completely separate
from us to have fun here. Is that it?

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.500
Yup.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.540
I'd be happy if you'd think of it that way.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:22.780
Yuki!

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.050
Please believe me, Yumi!

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.350
He shoved me into the car as soon
as we met at the school gate...

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.470
...and we came straight here.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:30.450
Yumi, let's go buy our tickets.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.350
Concerning ourselves with someone
like him is only a waste of time.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.120
Oh, yes, ma'am!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.390
Yes, good. Feel free to do as you please.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.360
We'll do whatever we want, too.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.230
Come on, Yukichi, let's go.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:44.870
Yes, sir.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.840
I'm sorry. Even my brother Yuki...

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.240
It's all right. Suguru-san strong-armed
him into coming, right?

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:55.240
But what could this be about?

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:01.050
He's not the sort of person to do
such a thing just to be a pest.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.180
Oh, so you're from Gunma.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.080
Yes.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.310
Is it just the two of you?

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.420
Yup, it's just the two of us.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:35.650
Wow, really?
Yup, it's just the two of us.

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:36.950
Wow, really?

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:40.350
What? Is it that suspicious for
two guys to be hanging out?

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:41.190
I'm hurt.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:41.860
You dummy.
I'm hurt.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:42.150
You dummy.

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:44.690
Pay attention to Suguru-san and you're
playing right into his hands.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.820
If you'd like, why don't you join us?

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:47.930
Nah...

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.200
Oh, that was fun!

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.800
Yumi, did you see it? That big frog?

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.900
Yes! At that moment,
I could not help myself and...

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:09.080
The restaurants are probably
at their most crowded right now.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:12.050
Let's go on one more ride and then eat.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.020
All right.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.520
O-Onee-sama?

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.420
Are you into roller coasters?

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.300
I'm not really...

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:25.930
I see, then Suguru-san will do.

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:28.600
Won't you please go ride with Yumi?

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:30.200
Okay.

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:31.740
O-Onee-sama!

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:34.180
I-I don't care about roller coasters...

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.980
I want to see you riding it.
You will do it, won't you?

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:42.250
But then, it doesn't have to be Kashiwagi-san...

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:43.650
Why not?

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:47.850
As a simple escort, there's
nothing wrong with me, right?

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:53.230
Or should Sacchan and I cordially wait for you?

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:54.130
What?

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:02.030
No! I absolutely don't want that!

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.910
I don't understand you, Kashiwagi-san.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:16.850
How so?

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.080
I don't know what kind of person
you are or what you're thinking.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.950
That's great.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.450
I'm insurance.

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:30.030
If something should happen,
I may become needed.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.960
Just think of me like that.

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.500
"Something"? Like what?

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.300
Oh, I don't know.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.700
Oh...

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.810
Is that "something" going to happen?

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:51.180
I would rather that I don't become needed.

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:53.350
All right.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.390
You seem unhappy, for all
that you're "all right" with it.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.410
Because!

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.930
Don't tell Sacchan about this conversation.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.430
I see.

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:07.030
So Kashiwagi-san came to the amusement park...

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:09.940
...out of concern for my dear sister.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:15.540
Kashiwagi-san is technically my
dear sister's cousin and betrothed.

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:20.180
He's known my dear sister since
before I ever met her,

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.670
and he notices things about her
faster than I notice them.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.320
That's why he came here
with Yuki, after all.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:31.590
And he is the person my
dear sister entrusted me to...

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:35.090
So... So...

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.610
You seemed like you really enjoyed yourself.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:53.040
What? You probably couldn't tell from below...

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:55.420
That's not true at all.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.850
I could tell you were screaming your head off.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.440
Onee-sama...

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:02.310
Your voice carried quite a bit.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:04.490
Even I could pick it out.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.720
You were awfully quiet, Suguru-san.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.030
Could it be that you were scared?

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.440
That was incredible, Onee-sama!

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:20.870
Hey!

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.220
Amazing! How amazing!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.600
Onee-sama, did you see that? They just...

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.060
Onee-sama?!

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.970
Onee-sama...

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:00.640
Onee-sama!

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:03.480
Can you stand?

00:12:03.850 --> 00:12:04.880
Kashiwagi-san...

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.120
It'll inconvenience these people,

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.020
so let's slip away quietly without
raising a commotion.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:10.280
Better that way, right?

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:11.150
Yes.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.230
I'm going to touch her for a bit.
Forgive me.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:14.630
What?

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:18.120
Yumi.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:24.800
Yumi!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.170
Let's go.

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.740
O-Okay.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.110
Onee-sama...

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:38.150
Yumi-chan, there's no need to cry.

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:42.490
Look's like Sacchan got overwhelmed
by the crowd or maybe a bit anemic.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.760
In other words, she felt faint
for a moment. That's all.

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:47.860
I am sorry, Yumi.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.020
Not at all.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:50.760
More importantly, are you all right?

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.930
It's just as Suguru-san said.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.340
You used to get ill on outings all the time,

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.130
ever since you were little.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:12:59.500
Yes.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:02.180
I guess I haven't been cured of it.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.540
How disappointing.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.150
Why don't you call it a day...

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:09.580
...and pick up where you
left off at another time?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.980
Oh, I'm fine now.

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:14.620
It's not for you.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:16.320
It's for us.

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:18.290
Even if we went on to have fun,

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.090
we'd be too worried about you to enjoy it.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:23.460
The amusement park isn't going anywhere.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:25.120
You can come again.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:27.930
What do you say?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.900
Three to one. It's settled.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.600
Oh, I can take that...

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.000
You take care of that.

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:52.390
You see, Sacchan...

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:56.190
...isn't very good at being
around a lot of people.

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.220
Oh, meaning strangers.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.800
You'd foreseen that this would happen, right?

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.230
Why didn't you stop her?

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:09.540
That's because Sacchan seemed
to be having a lot of fun.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:10.310
What?

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.050
She really looked like she was having fun.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.820
I've never seen Sacchan smile so much.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:19.420
But...

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.460
If you worry too much about
what might happen...

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.050
...and you eliminate all those things,
nothing will be left.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.220
I don't really understand.

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:31.130
Sacchan wants to do all sorts
of things with you, Yumi-chan.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:35.230
I thought it would be crueler
to keep her from that.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:37.290
That's what I meant.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:49.750
Are you all right, Onee-sama?

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:50.920
Thank you.
Are you all right, Onee-sama?

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:51.590
Are you all right, Onee-sama?

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.280
Yes, I am feeling quite well.

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.020
I am so sorry, Oba-sama.

00:14:57.090 --> 00:14:58.250
Oh, please.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:01.680
I'm the one who should be apologizing.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:03.730
Now, help yourself before it cools.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:04.490
Yes, ma'am.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:11.530
Oba-sama, were you
cooking or something?

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:12.760
Could you tell?

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.280
I was suddenly struck with
the urge right before lunch,

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.110
so I was baking some millefeuille.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.010
Why did you suddenly think of it?

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:24.880
You see, your father found a beautiful
autumn leaf for me yesterday.

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.850
I was so happy, it made me want to bake them.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:28.720
An autumn leaf...

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:30.350
That makes sense.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:36.130
You see, Yumi-chan, "millefeuille"...

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.860
...is a confection whose name
means "one thousand leaves."

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.930
Who could that be?

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:44.790
It's Iwamatsu-sensei.

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.040
You called the doctor?

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.840
I thought you would be far worse.

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:52.380
Since he is here, why not have
him look at you anyway?

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:55.240
But I'm fine now.

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:59.090
Please entertain our guests
for a short while for us.

00:15:59.090 --> 00:15:59.680
Certainly.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:04.990
Oh, if I may, I would like to
borrow your phone to call home.

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.590
The phone is outside this room
on the left side of the hall.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.120
Thank you very much.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.570
"We're finally alone, just the two of us."

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:28.670
I think it might be you who's thinking that.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:30.410
You certainly think highly of yourself.

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:32.580
Not really.

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:37.790
I just thought that maybe you
wanted to talk to me.

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:42.720
I hate you.

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:44.560
That's great.

00:16:45.700 --> 00:16:47.790
Why would he respond in that way?

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:52.110
You know, even if there's
someone you don't like,

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:55.370
you don't seem the type who'd
boldly say so to their face.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.850
So, the fact that you said
it in spite of it all...

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:02.340
...means you have pretty
strong feelings about me.

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:05.590
And that's something that makes me happy.

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:08.560
It would be harder if you didn't
think anything of me at all.

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:16.630
I think what I feel towards you is jealousy.

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:18.100
I know that.

00:17:18.770 --> 00:17:22.370
You love Sachiko-sama too, don't you?

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:23.060
I do.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.340
Then, why did you make her do that?

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.070
Do what?

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:31.280
You made Sachiko-sama say the
engagement was off, didn't you?

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:34.080
Oh, boy...

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:38.080
You're in love with Sachiko-sama, aren't you?

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:39.810
I can tell by watching you.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.640
But you...

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:43.320
But I?

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:48.430
You provoked her into breaking
off the engagement from her end.

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:51.220
I see.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:55.000
There are some things that you aren't seeing.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:55.970
What?

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:58.300
It's true, I love Sacchan.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.770
But there are all kinds of "love."

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:04.210
I love Sacchan, but I also love Yuki.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:07.300
And I also love you, Yumi-chan.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:10.480
But doesn't Sachiko-sama come first?

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.510
What does it mean to be first?

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:14.350
"I love my dog."

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.090
"I love the jelly from Maple Parlor."

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:20.330
You can't weigh them all equally, right?

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.350
But she's a person.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:25.900
Who do you love more?
Your father or your mother?

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:26.700
What?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.660
And what if we add Yuki to the mix?

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.370
What about Sacchan?

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:33.900
You can't decide who comes first, right?

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:36.380
I love Sacchan.

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:38.310
But I have no intention of marrying her.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:41.680
That's how I honestly feel right now.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:46.150
Are you not going to marry her
because it's Sachiko-sama?

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:49.010
Or are you not going to marry at all?

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:52.520
I wouldn't mind if it was with you.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:55.920
I'm sorry, but jokes like that aren't funny!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:57.990
Roger that. I'll stop.

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:01.220
One last thing.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.360
Defeating me won't give you victory.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:05.030
What?

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:10.010
Meaning, if you're jealous of me,
you've still got a long way to go.

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:12.210
Don't settle for what you've got now,

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.540
and aspire to attain something on a higher level.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.690
Looking at me like that won't do you any good.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:20.920
That's all the hint you're getting from me.

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:25.660
If you're not the enemy, what are you?

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:27.160
A fellow comrade.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:32.630
Yumi, Sachiko-san's asking for
you to come to her room...

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:33.600
What's wrong?

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:35.400
Oh, no, it's nothing.

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:37.530
Yumi?

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:52.810
Yumi.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:57.810
I was planning on returning
to the drawing room, but...

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:01.690
It's fine. Please stay in bed.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.460
Is something the matter?

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:15.570
I was jealous of Kashiwagi-san today.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:16.910
Oh, my.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:22.350
Because he easily does things that
I cannot do, even if I wanted to.

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:26.220
And he knows things so well
about you that I do not.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:31.650
How silly. There are also things that
you can do that Suguru-san cannot.

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:33.050
For example...

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:34.120
For example?

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:39.300
What I wanted to see right now was your smile.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:44.700
It was your hand that
I wanted holding mine in the car.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:46.600
Is that bad?

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:48.140
Bad? Hardly...

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:51.110
How much he knows about
me is bound to differ,

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:54.550
because the amount of time you and
I have known each other is different.

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:56.720
By that argument,

00:20:56.720 --> 00:21:00.490
I would have to be jealous of Yuki-san, too.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:01.890
Jealous of Yuki?

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:06.580
I came to comfort you, but you're
the one who has cheered me up.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.860
I'm sorry about today.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:12.800
I will be sure to go for a do-over!

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:16.640
Onee-sama, do not strain yourself
and think of it as a do-over.

00:21:16.640 --> 00:21:20.040
When we go next time, let's take it easy...

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:24.270
...with the mindset that it won't be a
problem even if you become ill again.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:26.750
You're right.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:29.270
I must have tried a little too hard today.

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:30.720
Yes.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:34.050
I should be more relaxed
in my approach, shouldn't I?

00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:37.190
It's not as if these are my last
moments with you, after all.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:38.280
Yes!

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:41.020
You are right...

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:54.510
Here is some millefeuille.

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:56.340
Please enjoy it with your parents.

00:21:58.250 --> 00:21:59.580
Millefeuille...

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:01.980
Don't drive so aggressively!

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:04.070
You complain too much, Yukichi.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:06.190
I wish I'd gotten Toko, after all.

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:07.120
Toko-chan?

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:08.150
Yup.

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.220
I invited Toko along first,

00:22:10.220 --> 00:22:12.320
but she declined, so Yukichi
moved to the top of the list.

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:14.590
So I'm a sub?

00:22:20.470 --> 00:22:22.300
"Mirufiiyu (millefeuille)"...

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:24.600
"Yu"..." Yumi"...

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.600
"Mi"..." Mirufiiyu (millefeuille)"...

00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:29.570
"Yu"...

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:47.830
A winterscape where even...
Machi no irodori sae doko

00:22:47.830 --> 00:22:52.600
...the town's colors seem forlorn somehow
to naku samishige na fuyu no keshiki

00:22:52.770 --> 00:22:56.600
I think of you, turning your back on me...
Senaka mise kaketeitta

00:22:56.600 --> 00:23:00.330
...and running off
anata o omou

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:05.310
There's a clear square pane...
Futari no aida ni wa

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:09.320
...between the two of us
toumei na shikakkei

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:12.090
It's misted over right now...
Ima wa kasunderu

00:23:12.090 --> 00:23:18.680
...with the crystals of sighs
tame-iki no kesshou de

00:23:19.260 --> 00:23:23.330
Window glass, window glass
Mado garasu mado garasu

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:29.300
It's clouded and I can't see you
Kumottete anata ga mienai no

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:35.100
Even though I know that you're there
Soko ni iru koto wa wakatteiru no ni

00:23:35.310 --> 00:23:39.250
Are you smiling? Are you crying?
Waratteru naiteru no

00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:45.250
I don't even care if you're frowning, let me see you
Shikamettsura demo ii kara misete

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:53.720
Wipe the glass from your side, too
Sochira no hou kara mo garasu o fuite

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:06.910
Preview

00:24:06.910 --> 00:24:09.810
Preview
Yuki, tonight's dinner is meatball curry.

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:11.880
Preview
Oh, that's Dad's favorite.

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:14.780
Preview
The meatballs at our house have cheese inside.

00:24:14.780 --> 00:24:15.720
Preview
What else are we having?

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:16.880
Preview
Salad, she said.

00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:20.350
Preview
I think Mother made the dressing
she saw on TV the other day.

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:22.060
Preview
With balsamic vinegar.

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:22.960
Preview
Hmm.

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:26.560
Preview
I never imagined Toko-chan would
be joining us for that dinner.

00:24:26.560 --> 00:24:27.060
Preview
An Unexpected Guest

00:24:27.060 --> 00:24:28.900
Preview
Next time, "An Unexpected Guest."
An Unexpected Guest

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:29.300
Preview
An Unexpected Guest

00:24:29.300 --> 00:24:31.500
Preview
Incidentally, specifically for
when we have curry,
An Unexpected Guest

00:24:31.500 --> 00:24:34.530
Preview
we mix brown rice, barley, and white rice.
An Unexpected Guest

00:24:34.530 --> 00:24:35.900
Preview
An Unexpected Guest
